### Clean Architecture template - API examples
### Works with the IntelliJ HTTP Client and the VS Code REST Client.
###
### The access token travels in the Authorization header. No endpoint writes a cookie, so there is
### no CSRF token, no refresh token and no logout call in this file.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@accessToken = replace-me
@todoId = replace-me
@email = demo-{{$randomUUID}}@example.com
@password = StrongPassword123!

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Register - public. Returns the access token in the body.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name register
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Login - public. Returns the same body as the registration.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name login
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Current user - the profile behind the token.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Create todo - the owner is the authenticated caller.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name createTodo
POST {{host}}/api/todos
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "title": "Write plan",
  "description": "Finish the architecture document",
  "dueDate": "2026-11-10"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("todoId", response.body.id);
%}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### List todos - page, size and the completion filter. The read model returns the
### newest todo first, so there is no sort parameter.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/todos?page=0&size=20
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/todos?completed=true
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/todos?completed=false
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Get todo
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/todos/{{todoId}}
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Update todo
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
PUT {{host}}/api/todos/{{todoId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

{
  "title": "Write plan (revised)",
  "description": "Updated through the HTTP client",
  "dueDate": "2026-11-12"
}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Complete todo - the response carries completed=true and completedAt.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/todos/{{todoId}}/complete
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Delete todo
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
DELETE {{host}}/api/todos/{{todoId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Error example - no token. Response: 401 ProblemDetail, code security.unauthorized
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/todos
Accept: application/problem+json

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Error example - an invalid body. Response: 400 ProblemDetail,
### code validation.failed with a fieldErrors array.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/problem+json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short"
}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Error example - wrong credentials. Response: 401 ProblemDetail,
### code auth.invalid-credentials. An unknown address gives the same answer.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/problem+json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "WrongPassword123!"
}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Error example - a todo of another user. Response: 404 ProblemDetail,
### code todo.not-found. The existence of a foreign todo is not disclosed.
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/api/todos/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Accept: application/problem+json
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Operational and documentation endpoints
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{host}}/actuator/health
Accept: application/json

###
GET {{host}}/v3/api-docs
Accept: application/json

###
GET {{host}}/scalar
Accept: text/html
